  "content": {
    "title": "North Carolina upset by VCU in March Madness overtime stunner, blowing 19-point lead",
    "text": "Updated March 19, 2026, 10:18 p.m. ETNo. 11 VCU upsets No. 6 seed North Carolina 82-78 in the first round of the NCAA Tournament on Thursday, March 19.The Tar Heels led by as many as 19 points during the game, but the Rams fought back for the sixth-largest comeback in March Madness history.Terrence Hill Jr. scored a 3-pointer for VCU, cutting into the Tar Heels' lead at 70-68. VCU went on a 12-0 scoring run.The score was tied at 75 with 8.7 seconds in the second half. Henri Veesaar had the ball for UNC but lost control of it and went out of bounds. VCU received the ball with 2.9 seconds but had the ball stolen by Seth Trimble. His shot was no good. The game is headed for overtime.Both teams were unable to score through the first three minutes of the overtime period. Nyk Lewis' layup put VCU in front for the first lead of overtime. Seth Trimble made a pair of free throws to even the game at 77.Trimble quickly found himself back at the free-throw line, where he made 1-of-2 to take a one-point lead for the Tar Heels. VCU would pull it out at the end with a clutch shot.The Rams would respond quickly as Terrence Hill made another three-pointer to put the Rams back in front at 80-78. Nyk Lewis also helped secure the victory with a pair of successful free throw attempts.Watch UNC vs VCU live with Sling TVThe Rams entered the game on Thursday having won 16 of their last 17 games, including the A-10 Conference Championship game to earn an automatic bid to the big dance. Their lone loss during that streak came against Saint Louis, a No. 9 seed in the NCAA Tournament as an at-large team. Largest first round comeback in March Madness historyVCU's victory over North Carolina was the largest in first round history and sixth-largest comeback in tournament history. See the full list here: Final: VCU 82, North Carolina 78No. 11 VCU upsets No. 6 seed North Carolina 82-78 in the first round of the NCAA Tournament on Thursday, May 19.Terrence Hill made another three-pointer to put the Rams back in front by two points at 80-78. Nyk Lewis also helped secure the victory with a pair of successful free throw attempts. VCU and North Carolina remain tiedBoth teams were unable to score through the first three minutes of the overtime period. Nyk Lewis' layup put VCU in front for the first lead of overtime. Seth Trimble made a pair of free throws to even the game at 77. North Carolina and VCU headed for overtimeThe game was tied at 75 with 8.7 seconds in the second half. Henri Veesaar had the ball for UNC but lost control of it and went out of bounds. VCU received the ball with 2.9 seconds but had the ball stolen by Seth Trimble. His shot was no good. The game is headed for overtime. VCU attempts comeback against UNCVCU is on a 12-0 run over the last two minutes of the period. North Carolina leads VCU 70-68 with 3:56 left in the second half after Terrence Hill Jr. scored a long-range shot. VCU continues to battleVCU continues to battle with North Carolina throughout the second half. The teams have scored 28 points each in the period. The Tar Heels remain in front of the Rams 67-56 with 7:30 left in regulation. VCU struggles to keep up with UNCNorth Carolina leads VCU 61-47 with 11:30 left in the second half. Henri Veesaar leads the game with 20 points and seven rebounds (five on defense). Seth Trimble has contributed with 12 points, five rebounds and four assists. VCU's Lazar Djokovic has produced 15 points and four rebounds, while Terrence Hill Jr. has scored 17 points. Both have played over 23 minutes tonight. UNC leads VCU early in second halfThe Tarheels start the second half outscoring 12-9 in the first few minutes of the game. The Rams trail the Tar Heels 51-37. Herni Veesaar has compiled 17 points and seven rebounds. He is still just 1-for-5 from the three-point line. Halftime: North Carolina 39, VCU 28North Carolina enters the locker room at halftime with a 39-28 point lead at halftime.The Tarheels have led the game by as many as 15 points in the first half. The Rams never held a lead larger than three.Henri Veesaar had 13 points and five rebounds in the first half for UNC. Terrence Hill Jr. produced 11 points for VCU. North Carolina pulling away from VCUDerek Dixon leads North Carolina with six points after shooting 2-for-2 from the three-point line. The Tarheels have put together a 7-0 scoring run to lead VCU 24-18 with 7:43 left in the first half. UNC's Hubert Davis seeks more second-chance scoring opportunitiesNorth Carolina coach Hubert Davis told CBS sideline reporter Tracy Wolfson that he wants the Tarheels to continue to play at the fast pace with VCU, but would want to see his team get more rebounds and second-chance scoring opportunities. VCU and North Carolina tied at 13VCU and North Carolina are tied at 13 with 11:33 left in the first half. Both teams are shooting a combined 1-11 from the three-point line. VCU's Terrence Hill Jr. hit the first 3-pointer of the game off an assist from Michael Belle. VCU leads North Carolina earlyVCU leads North Carolina 8-5 with 15:36 left in the first half. UNC went nearly three minutes without scoring. North Carolina starting lineup vs. VCUSeth Trimble, Derek Dixon, Luka Bogavac, Jarin Stevenson and Henri Veesaar will start for North Carolina today vs. VCU. VCU starting lineup vs. North CarolinaBrandon Jennings, Nyk Lewis, Jadrian Tracey, Barry Evans and Lazar Djokovic make up the starting lineup for VCU today vs. UNC.What TV channel is North Carolina vs VCU basketball on today?TV channel: TNTStreaming: Sling TVNorth Carolina vs. VCU will air nationally on TNT, with Ian Eagle, Bill Raftery, Grant Hill and Tracy Wolfson on the call. Streaming options for the game include Sling TV, which carries TNT.UNC vs VCU March Madness game start time todayDate: Thursday, March 19Time: 6:50 p.m. ETLocation: Bon Secours Wellness Arena (Greenville, South Carolina)The Tar Heels and Rams' game is scheduled to begin at 6:50 p.m. ET from Bon Secours Wellness Arena in Greenville on March 19.No. 6 North Carolina vs No. 11 VCU predictionsJohn Leuzzi: VCUEhsan Kassim: North CarolinaAustin Curtright: VCUCraig Meyer: VCUNorth Carolina vs VCU oddsOdds courtesy of BetMGM as of Wednesday, March 18Spread: North Carolina (-2.5)Over/under: 152.5Moneyline: North Carolina (-150) | VCU (+125)",
